<main>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <a class="back-link" href="/resources">&larr; Back to Resources</a>
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">A Workbook For Men</span>
          <h1>Carry the Weight,<br><em>Not the Damage</em></h1>
          <p class="lead">Most men were handed three instructions growing up: handle it, don't make it a
          thing, and don't let them see you sweat. Useful in an emergency. Expensive as a way of life.
          This is a workbook for the man who looks fine on paper and knows something underneath isn't.</p>

          <div class="price-row">
            <span class="price">$14</span>
            <span class="price-note">27 pages · instant PDF download</span>
          </div>

          <div class="button-row">
            <a class="btn btn-gold payhip-buy-button" href="https://payhip.com/b/6r5wg" data-theme="none" data-product="6r5wg">Get the Workbook</a>
            <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#inside">See What's Inside</a>
          </div>

          <div class="spec">
            <span>Written by David Robles, LMSW</span>
            <span>U.S. Army veteran</span>
            <span>Print at home or use on a tablet</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal hero-art">
          <img src="/images/carry-the-weight-cover.webp" width="920" height="920" loading="eager"
               alt="Cover of Carry the Weight, Not the Damage, a men's mental health workbook by David Robles, LMSW. Practical tools for stress, anger, pressure, and the stuff you don't talk about. 27 pages.">
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHO IT'S FOR -->
  <section class="section" id="who">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="what-is-grid" style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.15fr .85fr; gap:64px; align-items:start;">
        <div class="reveal prose">
          <span class="eyebrow">Who This Is For</span>
          <h2>You are functioning. That was never the question.</h2>
          <p>You go to work. You handle what needs handling. Nobody looking at your life would say
          anything is wrong with it. And still there is the short fuse over nothing, the numbness that
          shows up in your own living room, and the three in the morning meeting your brain schedules
          without asking.</p>
          <p>Most material written for this either treats you like you are fragile or tells you to be
          harder. This does neither. It gives you the same practical tools used in a therapy room, in
          plain language, without an appointment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal">
          <div class="quote-card">
